    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear mandate: exploit stolen base opportunities and capitalize on favorable matchups against mid-rotation arms. **Corbin Carroll** (79.76) and **Brice Turang** (70.39) headline our lineup as the premier plays. Both benefit from the \"Slow SP Delivery\" metric, which significantly elevates their stolen base ceiling against Roki Sasaki and Zebby Matthews, respectively. **Corbin Carroll** in particular is locked in for an elite performance, as the synergy between his projected #2 spot in the order and the matchup dynamics provides the highest floor on the team. **Mickey Moniak** (68.44) also warrants attention; while his raw base projection is modest, a massive 14% boost from platoon splits against Leahy makes him a high-leverage start, even with the modest penalty for Leahy\u2019s pickoff ability.\n\nOur optimization process was most tested at the 1B/MI/UTIL spots. **Josh Naylor** (46.99) and **Max Muncy** (49.99) were narrowly included over **Cole Young** (33.73). While **Cole Young** possesses upside, his score was suppressed by a difficult matchup against Drew Rasmussen (3.19 xERA) and a poor park factor, making him a clear \"below floor\" option relative to the rest of the infield. We are keeping a close eye on **Austin Riley** (51.11), who remains a marginal start; he faces the dual threat of a sub-4.00 xERA in Max Fried and a 38% rain risk that could lead to an early exit or cold swings. We remain cautious of **Zach McKinstry** (47.10) as well, given the elite catcher arm behind the plate today, which severely caps his stolen base potential despite his late-order role.\n\nBeyond the starters, we are monitoring the health of our bench depth, as **James Wood** and **Trevor Story** remain sidelined on the IL, leaving us reliant on our current active personnel. We are also tracking **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** for potential spot-start utility as the week progresses, but for today, the focus remains on leveraging the speed of **Corbin Carroll** and **Brice Turang** to move the needle in the SB category. **Gabriel Moreno** (60.56) and **Seiya Suzuki** (59.59) provide solid, reliable production, while **Isaac Paredes** (56.66) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (50.12) round out a roster optimized to maximize daily efficiency scores while preserving our total game caps.",
